        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1678">

                <pb facs="1425" n="1321" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg1321"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 367.114M69/152.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 234.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-06-28">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 28, 1912</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my cablegram of May 13,
                    regarding American consular jurisdiction in the case of the captain of the
                    steamship <hi rendition="#italic">Texas</hi> at the time of that vessel’s
                    sinking in Smyrna harbor on April 29 last, and to your cabled instruction of
                    June 5, I have the honor herewith to enclose copies of the notes verbales
                    transmitted by the Embassy to the Porte in pursuance of your instructions.</p>
                <p>I have also to transmit herewith copy of a memorandum which I personally handed
                    to the Porte on the 11th of May when first the attention of the Ottoman
                    Government was called to the matter, according to your cabled instructions of
                    May 8.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. W. Rockhill</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>





